=== FACTOR 1: confounding-structure shift, no measurement problem ===
  delta |coupling A-B|   n prog   replic    AUC replication
    0.0        0.045     1730    0.957      0.943 (sd 0.021)
    0.1        0.124     1796    0.909      0.926 (sd 0.024)
    0.2        0.302     1810    0.858      0.884 (sd 0.049)
    0.3        0.498     1813    0.843      0.842 (sd 0.076)
    0.4        0.796     1841    0.450      0.609 (sd 0.109)

  delta=0 is the exchangeable-cohorts FLOOR: the AUC the anchor earns from
  signal strength alone, with no artifact of any kind present.

=== FACTOR 2: measurement corruption, no composition shift (delta=0) ===
   frac     replic  AUC repl. corrupt/clean AUC detect corrupt
   0.25      0.939      0.925  0.89/0.95          0.615
   0.50      0.892      0.887  0.66/0.95          0.733
   0.75      0.799      0.933  0.23/0.94          0.859

  AUC-detect is scored against the genes we actually corrupted (ground truth).

=== VERDICT ===
  floor (exchangeable cohorts)      AUC = 0.943
  max composition shift, no noise   AUC = 0.943  (+0.000 over floor)
  max corruption, no shift          AUC = 0.933  (-0.010 over floor)
  corrupted-gene detection          AUC = 0.859

  If both factors raise the AUC above the floor, the gate is a detector of
  anchor-relationship discordance from EITHER cause -- it cannot be described
  as a measurement-fidelity test, and the observational AUCs in Table 4 must
  be read against the floor rather than against 0.5.

